// =============================================================================
// PILOT-identity-join-test.kql  |  The 5-minute flagship confirmation
//
// Run this in the Eventhouse / KQL Database that Workspace Monitoring created in
// your pilot workspace (Fabric portal -> workspace -> KQL DB -> New KQL Queryset).
// Run each numbered block top-to-bottom and paste the returns back to the assistant.
//
// PREREQS (all must be true or the match returns empty for a boring reason):
//   - Workspace Monitoring is ON for the workspace (Settings -> Monitoring -> On)
//   - A semantic model in it refreshes THROUGH your on-prem gateway
//   - You clicked Refresh on that model at least once in the last hour
//   - You copied 2-3 RequestId GUIDs from the gateway host's newest
//     QueryStartReport*.csv (RequestId column), at:
//     C:\Windows\ServiceProfiles\PBIEgwService\AppData\Local\Microsoft\
//         On-premises data gateway\Report
// =============================================================================


// ---- (1) PEEK: does the monitoring table have any recent rows? --------------
// Empty here => monitoring hasn't captured activity yet: wait 10-15 min after a
// refresh and retry. Paste what this returns (even "empty").
PowerBIDatasetsWorkspace
| where Timestamp > ago(1d)
| take 20
| project Timestamp, OperationId, OperationName, ExecutingUser, ItemName


// ---- (2) THE MATCH: gateway RequestId -> user + dataset (the flagship test) --
// Replace the GUID with one you copied from the gateway log. Run once per
// RequestId (try 2-3). Rows back with ExecutingUser + ItemName populated = the
// core promise is PROVEN live. Paste exactly what returns for each.
PowerBIDatasetsWorkspace
| where OperationId == "PASTE-YOUR-REQUESTID-HERE"
| project Timestamp, OperationId, OperationName,
          ExecutingUser, ItemName, ItemId, WorkspaceId


// ---- (3) SCHEMA: confirm the real column names in YOUR tenant ----------------
// Confirms the desk-verified column-name claim in 01_identity_join.kql's header
// block (PowerBIDatasetsWorkspace schema). Paste all.
PowerBIDatasetsWorkspace
| getschema
| project ColumnName, ColumnType


// ---- (4) OPTIONAL, if the trial capacity is still throttle-slow --------------
// A narrowed monitoring-table scan (NOT the full gateway↔monitoring join --
// that requires landing the gateway logs into the Eventhouse first; see
// starter/kql/01_identity_join.kql): last 15 min, single workspace, so it
// stays under a trial Spark/KQL throttle.
// Set the workspace GUID (from block 2's WorkspaceId), then run.
let lookback = 15m;
let ws = "PASTE-YOUR-WORKSPACE-GUID-HERE";
PowerBIDatasetsWorkspace
| where Timestamp > ago(lookback)
| where WorkspaceId == ws
| where OperationName in ("QueryEnd", "ExecutionMetrics", "RefreshEnd")
| project Timestamp, OperationId, ExecutingUser, ItemName, DurationMs, CpuTimeMs
| order by Timestamp desc
| take 25

// Redaction: ExecutingUser is a real UPN and ItemName may be a real dataset name.
// Redact to user@... / Dataset-A if you prefer -- the assistant only needs to see
// THAT the fields populated and WHICH RequestIds matched, not the actual values.
